Changelog: 07-11-2026 21:19:23

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:23:23

Breaking. The window is built as RPCS3 Manager's (owner, 07-11-2026: RPCS3 Manager's design is every manager's). The app
has no Play button any more: a game is started from Steam, and a double-click on a game no longer starts it. Settings…
is gone: PPSSPP's settings are in the Settings tab. Covers… is now Steam artwork…, Update Game Mode is now Update Steam,
the Game Mode column is In Steam and the In Game Mode box is Available in Steam. The messages box under the table is
gone: what the app says is in the Log tab.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:23:23

Added. The header has the Refresh pill and the boxes, PPSSPP version, Your games and Available in Steam, spread over the
window's width, with the app's state beside the title. Under the introduction, which links to PPSSPP's release notes and
to the wiki, stands a row of action pills: PPSSPP Install, PPSSPP Uninstall and Games Rename, which opens the Rename
files window. The state of each follows in two lines, then three tabs: Your games (the table with PPSSPP settings,
Remove game…, Steam artwork… and Update Steam, and a link that opens Steam's library), Settings and Log. What the app
says and does goes to its log, ~/.local/share/ps5-ppsspp-manager/ps5-ppsspp-manager.log (turned over at 1 MB), shown in
the Log tab; install.sh --uninstall keeps it, --purge removes it. The tabs, the pills and the choice boxes take RPCS3
Manager's style.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:23:23

Added. The PPSSPP line under the pills says only the state, in the words every manager uses (owner, 07-11-2026): "Not
installed." with "Install it with the Install button." under it, or "Installed." with "Uninstall with the Uninstall
button." under it. The version installed, what Install takes, another version than the app brings, and a newer PPSSPP
are in the line's tooltip; another version and a newer PPSSPP also go to the log, once.

Changelog: 06-11-2026 22:49:44

Fixed. Installing the port preserves the standalone file renamer and its data; release messages describe the pinned
build without implying PS5 hardware validation.

Changelog: 06-11-2026 22:39:30

Added. Ported PPSSPP Manager for PSP games with console-suite launchers, settings, and Game Mode shortcuts.
